  "id": "felt-sense",
  "term": "felt sense",
  "definition": "A felt sense is a bodily, experiential sense of something that can be noticed and attended to in somatic or therapeutic work. In this use, giving it compassionate attention allows the sensation to respond and change over time, sometimes moving toward a felt shift.",
